        <headline>SYSTEMS BLEED AND PRESSURISATION DAILY REVIEW</headline>
        <description>BACKGROUND: ACMS REVIEW SHOWS RH BLEED PX TO BE LOW DURING TAXI  (3 PSI TAXI).

HEALTH CHECK REQUIRED.

ACTION:  
1. GAIN ACCESS TO THE #2 BLEED COMPONENTS.  

2. USING PNEUMATIC TESTING KIT (P/N 1945-04-08 ) PERFORM A COMPLETE PNEUMATIC HEALTH CHECK OF THE #2 BLEED COMPONENTS IAW AMM 36-11-00.
    
* RECORD THE RESULTS ON THE ATTACHED RA851 FORM AND SUBMIT TO BLEEDREVIEW@RYANAIR.COM  
    
** RECORD THE SERIAL NUMBER OF THE TEST KIT USED ON THE RA851 FORM ALSO.
    
3. INSPECT #2 HSR FOR RUPTURED REVERSE FLOW DIAPHRAGM.

4. CLOSELY INSPECT RH PRSOV FOR NOTCHY BEHAVIOUR, INABILITY TO REMAIN OPEN AND ACTUATOR BODY LEAKAGE.

5. LEAK CHECK ALL RH HSR / HSV / PCCV / BAR SENSE LINES USING SUITABLE LEAK CHECK SPRAY. SPECIAL FOCUS ON  THE FOLLOWING SENSE LINES OR FITTINGS:     
- HSR SUPPLY PRESSURE SENSE LINE (BETWEEN 9TH STAGE AND HSR) 
- HSV CONTROL PRESSURE SENSE LINE (BETWEEN HSR AND HSV)
 
6. IF NFF, REPLACE THE #2 HSR IAW 36-11-07/401.

7. RETURN THE AIRCRAFT TO SERVICE.

**AIRCRAFT IS EQUIPPED WITH ACMS - NO BLEED SHEETS WILL BE REQUIRED.  

**PLEASE ENSURE THAT ALL ELECTRICAL (WHERE APPLICABLE) AND PNEUMATIC FITTINGS / COMPONENTS DISTURBED DURING ABOVE WORKS ARE RE-INSTATED TO CORRECT CONFIGURATION AFTER WORKS.</description>
